 * A declared REST proxy route carries its `(tool, action)` statically, so
 * it can be checked against the same `PUBLIC_READ_ACTIONS` allow-list the
 * tool door uses — no request body to parse. Only routes that are a pure
 * proxy are declared, so this widens the transport, never the policy.
